  "@context": "https://doi.org/10.5063/schema/codemeta-2.0",
  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "SPMD",
  "description": "Symmetric time pair matching is a self-controlled method that is designed to allow estimation of the causal effect of a transient exposure (such as vaccinations) on a potentially recurrent outcome. It automatically adjust for all time-invariant confounders and time effects using a special kind of pair matching. As such, only very minimal assumptions have to be made about how time influences the exposure or outcome probability.",
  "name": "SPMD: Symmetric Time Pair Matching for Causal Inference",
  "relatedLink": "https://robindenz1.github.io/SPMD/",
